1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,889
Imagine standing at the back
of a padel court,

2
00:00:02,889 --> 00:00:07,161
pinned against the glass while two
opponents smash volleys at your feet.

3
00:00:07,511 --> 00:00:11,412
Every ball feels like a blur, your
racket clips the wall,

4
00:00:11,412 --> 00:00:14,103
and the point ends before you can react.

5
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:18,593
Today, I will show you the 5 mistakes
destroying your defense,

6
00:00:18,593 --> 00:00:22,602
and the court science to turn every
wall ball into an attack.

7
00:00:22,953 --> 00:00:27,732
In padel, over 80 percent of points are won
by the team controlling the net.

8
00:00:28,081 --> 00:00:32,177
Defending is not about surviving
indefinitely at the baseline.

9
00:00:32,527 --> 00:00:37,362
Defense has one goal: neutralize the
attack, evict opponents from the net,

10
00:00:37,362 --> 00:00:38,458
and take it back.

11
00:00:38,808 --> 00:00:43,173
Most players fail because they bring
habits from tennis, squash,

12
00:00:43,173 --> 00:00:46,061
or pickleball into an
enclosed glass court.

13
00:00:46,411 --> 00:00:49,590
Here are the 5 traps keeping you
locked at the back.

14
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:55,376
The hardest place to defend in padel is the
90-degree corner between the rear and

15
00:00:55,376 --> 00:00:56,105
side glass.

16
00:00:56,455 --> 00:01:02,151
When a ball enters this corner, it hits both
walls, creating a double glass rebound.

17
00:01:02,501 --> 00:01:06,768
The fatal mistake is running straight into
the corner facing the glass,

18
00:01:06,768 --> 00:01:09,968
waiting for the ball to hit both
walls before turning.

19
00:01:10,318 --> 00:01:14,659
By then, the ball bounces off the second
wall directly into your hip,

20
00:01:14,659 --> 00:01:16,334
pinning you with zero room.

21
00:01:16,684 --> 00:01:21,689
Trying to pivot on high-traction turf with
your foot planted twists your knee,

22
00:01:21,689 --> 00:01:25,047
creating dangerous rotational
shear on your meniscus.

23
00:01:25,397 --> 00:01:28,810
To fix this, read which glass the
ball strikes first.

24
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:33,149
If the ball hits the side wall first,
that is an opening double.

25
00:01:33,499 --> 00:01:37,118
Open the door immediately: take
a mini split-step,

26
00:01:37,118 --> 00:01:40,454
pivot your hips 180 degrees
with flexed knees,

27
00:01:40,454 --> 00:01:43,931
and maintain 1 meter of
clearance from the glass.

28
00:01:44,281 --> 00:01:48,697
Think of a revolving door: turn with the
curve, never fight against it.

29
00:01:49,047 --> 00:01:52,887
If the ball hits the back wall first,
that is a closing double.

30
00:01:53,237 --> 00:01:55,178
Do not spin in circles here.

31
00:01:55,529 --> 00:01:59,832
Keep your chest facing the side wall,
take two small steps forward,

32
00:01:59,832 --> 00:02:02,996
and catch the rebound as it
leaves the back glass.

33
00:02:03,345 --> 00:02:08,994
Train this with the Open-the-Door drill: start
with gentle feeds for 4 sets of 10

34
00:02:08,994 --> 00:02:12,369
side-first corner balls before
adding match pace.

35
00:02:12,719 --> 00:02:17,107
Pivot on the balls of your feet with soft
knees before glass contact,

36
00:02:17,107 --> 00:02:19,802
guiding the rebound smoothly
down the line.

37
00:02:20,152 --> 00:02:22,810
When heavy smashes rain down from the net,

38
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:27,384
your natural instinct is to back up until
your heels touch the back glass.

39
00:02:27,734 --> 00:02:29,633
This is called the safety illusion.

40
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:33,130
You think standing farther away
gives you more time,

41
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:35,743
but hugging the glass
destroys your defense.

42
00:02:36,093 --> 00:02:38,445
First, you have zero backswing room,

43
00:02:38,445 --> 00:02:42,514
so your paddle smacks the glass and
you push weak balls forward.

44
00:02:42,864 --> 00:02:47,511
Second, tempered glass rebounds about 70
percent of incoming speed,

45
00:02:47,511 --> 00:02:50,928
launching deep shots 1 to 2
meters into the court.

46
00:02:51,278 --> 00:02:55,673
If you are standing against the wall, the
ball rebounds behind your body.

47
00:02:56,023 --> 00:03:01,771
Third, standing against the wall creates a
massive 7-meter empty desert between you

48
00:03:01,771 --> 00:03:04,919
and the net, giving opponents
easy drop shots.

49
00:03:05,269 --> 00:03:09,796
The fix is anchoring yourself in the
defensive sweet spot: 0.

50
00:03:09,796 --> 00:03:14,762
8 meters behind the service line, and 1
meter in from the side glass.

51
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:19,571
Standing here is like a soccer goalkeeper
positioning off the goal line.

52
00:03:19,921 --> 00:03:23,398
When a short ball comes, step
forward across the line.

53
00:03:23,748 --> 00:03:27,685
When a deep ball comes, track
backward with crossover steps,

54
00:03:27,685 --> 00:03:31,364
keeping a 1-meter deceleration
buffer from the back wall.

55
00:03:31,714 --> 00:03:35,533
Strike it at waist height as it
rebounds forward into the court.

56
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:41,683
Train this with the Service-Line Tether drill:
mark your sweet spot with cones 0.

57
00:03:41,683 --> 00:03:43,947
8 meters behind the service line.

58
00:03:44,297 --> 00:03:50,298
Have a feeder alternate between a short ball
and a deep glass ball for 4 sets of 8

59
00:03:50,298 --> 00:03:50,804
cycles.

60
00:03:51,153 --> 00:03:56,567
Strike the short ball, and glide backward using
controlled crossover steps to touch

61
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:57,212
your cone.

62
00:03:57,562 --> 00:04:02,938
Track both ball and wall, letting the glass feed
the rebound right into your strike

63
00:04:02,938 --> 00:04:03,258
zone.

64
00:04:03,608 --> 00:04:08,675
When players are pinned deep under heavy
pressure, they panic and blast a flat,

65
00:04:08,675 --> 00:04:11,779
60-mile-per-hour missile
straight at net players.

66
00:04:12,129 --> 00:04:15,478
This is the single most
self-destructive shot in padel.

67
00:04:15,828 --> 00:04:21,439
At 7 meters away, net players hold solid
composite rackets with no strings.

68
00:04:21,789 --> 00:04:26,768
A hard flat shot hits their racket and
rebounds with devastating pace,

69
00:04:26,768 --> 00:04:29,362
giving them an instant reflex winner.

70
00:04:29,712 --> 00:04:35,308
Attempting flat speed-ups from deep court
increases your unforced errors by over

71
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:35,792
4-fold.

72
00:04:36,142 --> 00:04:41,733
Firing hard at net players is like throwing
rocks at a tank: you only give them the

73
00:04:41,733 --> 00:04:43,331
ammunition to crush you.

74
00:04:43,681 --> 00:04:47,414
The true weapon of padel defense
is the high reset lob.

75
00:04:47,765 --> 00:04:53,017
In professional padel, players choose the lob
in over 60 percent of defensive

76
00:04:53,017 --> 00:04:58,605
transitions, keeping the rally alive and
neutralizing the attack nearly two-thirds

77
00:04:58,605 --> 00:04:59,413
of the time.

78
00:04:59,763 --> 00:05:05,920
A proper defensive lob arches 5 to 8
meters into the air, creating 3.

79
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:06,623
5 to 4.

80
00:05:06,623 --> 00:05:09,086
5 seconds of flight hang time.

81
00:05:09,435 --> 00:05:12,209
Those 4 seconds break opponents' rhythm,

82
00:05:12,209 --> 00:05:15,592
force both volleyers to sprint
7 meters backward,

83
00:05:15,592 --> 00:05:18,096
and give you time to capture the net.

84
00:05:18,447 --> 00:05:22,673
To hit it, bend your knees, open your
paddle face 25 degrees,

85
00:05:22,673 --> 00:05:26,831
and lift smoothly from your legs
without snapping your wrist.

86
00:05:27,181 --> 00:05:32,561
Practice the Stopwatch Lob drill: hit lobs from
the baseline with a partner timing

87
00:05:32,561 --> 00:05:33,858
the ball in the air.

88
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:39,834
Do 4 sets of 10 repetitions, counting only
lobs that hang for at least 3.

89
00:05:39,834 --> 00:05:42,571
5 seconds and land in the back third.

90
00:05:42,921 --> 00:05:45,688
Sometimes opponents anticipate your lob,

91
00:05:45,688 --> 00:05:49,940
standing 3 to 4 meters back from the
net with overheads cocked.

92
00:05:50,289 --> 00:05:55,729
Or you play in an indoor club with a low ceiling
where sky-high lobs are restricted.

93
00:05:56,079 --> 00:06:01,083
When amateurs cannot lob, they usually hit a
medium-pace drive right at the

94
00:06:01,083 --> 00:06:02,202
opponent's chest.

95
00:06:02,552 --> 00:06:07,608
This lets net players lean forward and punch an
aggressive angle off the side fence.

96
00:06:07,958 --> 00:06:12,246
The secret weapon here is the chiquita,
which means "the little one."

97
00:06:12,596 --> 00:06:18,368
A chiquita is a slow, dipping slice that crosses
inches over the net and dies right

98
00:06:18,368 --> 00:06:20,361
at your opponent's shoelaces.

99
00:06:20,711 --> 00:06:22,642
Padel net height is 0.

100
00:06:22,642 --> 00:06:24,572
88 meters at the center.

101
00:06:24,923 --> 00:06:30,171
If opponents contact the ball above the net,
they can spike downward into the glass.

102
00:06:30,521 --> 00:06:33,077
When your chiquita dips below net height,

103
00:06:33,077 --> 00:06:36,729
physics forces them to volley upward
just to clear the tape.

104
00:06:37,079 --> 00:06:42,092
The instant they hit that floating upward ball,
your defense flips into an attack.

105
00:06:42,442 --> 00:06:46,636
To execute it, cushion the ball with a
compact slice backswing,

106
00:06:46,636 --> 00:06:49,781
applying gentle backspin so it
dips immediately.

107
00:06:50,131 --> 00:06:55,315
Most importantly, only advance once the ball
visibly dips below net tape height.

108
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:59,101
Take two quick steps forward into
the transition zone,

109
00:06:59,101 --> 00:07:03,537
split-step with paddle chest-high, and
pounce on their floating volley.

110
00:07:03,887 --> 00:07:08,435
Train this with the Shoelace Drop
drill: place target hoops 1.

111
00:07:08,435 --> 00:07:10,095
5 meters behind the net.

112
00:07:10,445 --> 00:07:16,693
Feed balls from the baseline, alternating
between high reset lobs and soft dipping

113
00:07:16,693 --> 00:07:19,704
chiquitas, aiming for 4 sets of 12 reps.

114
00:07:20,053 --> 00:07:25,554
The padel court is 10 meters wide, and opponents
love driving the ball straight down

115
00:07:25,554 --> 00:07:27,690
the center seam between partners.

116
00:07:28,041 --> 00:07:33,844
Amateur pairs either both freeze, letting the
ball roll off the glass, or both swing,

117
00:07:33,844 --> 00:07:36,745
clashing rackets and risking
hand injuries.

118
00:07:37,095 --> 00:07:42,614
Even worse, when one player gets pulled wide
into a corner, the other stands still,

119
00:07:42,614 --> 00:07:45,308
leaving a 4-meter canyon down the middle.

120
00:07:45,658 --> 00:07:50,462
Spatial tracking shows that elite pairs
move as a synchronized unit,

121
00:07:50,462 --> 00:07:53,317
connected by an invisible 3-meter string.

122
00:07:53,667 --> 00:07:56,625
When your partner slides wide
to the right corner,

123
00:07:56,625 --> 00:07:59,235
you must slide right to seal
the center seam.

124
00:07:59,585 --> 00:08:03,340
Next, establish middle priority
before the point begins.

125
00:08:03,689 --> 00:08:08,434
The default rule is forehand in the middle:
for two right-handed players,

126
00:08:08,434 --> 00:08:13,885
the left-side player takes contested center
balls because their forehand has natural

127
00:08:13,885 --> 00:08:14,462
leverage.

128
00:08:14,813 --> 00:08:19,934
If you are playing cross-court, the player
diagonally opposite the hitter covers the

129
00:08:19,934 --> 00:08:20,296
drive.

130
00:08:20,645 --> 00:08:26,416
Above all, enforce the early call-or-yield rule:
the moment the ball crosses the net

131
00:08:26,416 --> 00:08:27,706
tape, shout "Mine."

132
00:08:28,057 --> 00:08:33,036
If no call is heard, the secondary partner
must immediately yield and clear the

133
00:08:33,036 --> 00:08:34,094
hitting corridor.

134
00:08:34,444 --> 00:08:39,899
Calling early eliminates hesitation and lets
your partner step aside to cover the

135
00:08:39,899 --> 00:08:40,631
next angle.

136
00:08:40,981 --> 00:08:46,473
Practice the Center Calling drill: have a
feeder fire rapid groundstrokes down the

137
00:08:46,473 --> 00:08:48,789
center line for 4 sets of 12 balls.

138
00:08:49,139 --> 00:08:54,027
Call "Mine" while the ball is airborne over
the net, scoop a defensive lob,

139
00:08:54,027 --> 00:08:57,886
and coordinate seamless coverage
without a single collision.

140
00:08:58,235 --> 00:09:03,803
To lock these 5 fixes into your muscle memory,
follow this simple weekly court plan.

141
00:09:04,153 --> 00:09:10,323
In session one, spend 15 minutes on corner
glass reads: 4 sets of 10 reps of the

142
00:09:10,323 --> 00:09:15,502
Open-the-Door drill, alternating
side-first and back-first rebounds.

143
00:09:15,853 --> 00:09:22,548
In session two, dedicate 15 minutes to
transition mastery: 4 sets of 10 Stopwatch

144
00:09:22,548 --> 00:09:26,712
Lobs and 4 sets of 8
Chiquita-and-Pounce sequences.

145
00:09:27,061 --> 00:09:31,113
During match play, make the sweet
spot your home base: 0.

146
00:09:31,113 --> 00:09:36,562
8 meters behind the service line, connected
to your partner by that invisible

147
00:09:36,562 --> 00:09:36,981
string.

148
00:09:37,331 --> 00:09:42,076
Always complete an 8-minute warm-up with
dynamic ankle calf lunges,

149
00:09:42,076 --> 00:09:47,868
lateral hip openers, and standing thoracic
spine rotations with your racket across

150
00:09:47,868 --> 00:09:48,915
your shoulders.

151
00:09:49,265 --> 00:09:53,798
If you feel sudden knee locking, sharp
wrist shock after contact,

152
00:09:53,798 --> 00:09:56,340
or cannot bear weight on your ankle,

153
00:09:56,340 --> 00:10:01,766
stop immediately and see a sports
physiotherapist or sports medicine physician.

154
00:10:02,117 --> 00:10:06,256
Padel defense is not about panic,
scrambling, or hitting harder.

155
00:10:06,605 --> 00:10:11,163
Master the geometry of the glass,
command the defensive sweet spot,

156
00:10:11,163 --> 00:10:14,179
and let the walls become
your greatest ally.

157
00:10:14,179 --> 00:10:15,586
See you on the court.
